; A 128 BIT VALUE DOUBLED IN THE FIELD CMAC USES  which is a left shift by
; one across sixteen big endian bytes  followed by a conditional exclusive or
; of 0x87 into the last byte when the bit that fell off the first was set;
;
; NIST SP 800_38B section 6 point 1; It is exactly the shape of aes/xtime one
; byte wide: double  and reduce by the field's polynomial if the top bit was
; set; The polynomial here is x^128 plus x^7 plus x^2 plus x plus 1  whose low
; byte is 0x87  where xtime's is 0x1b;
;
; THE REDUCTION IS UNCONDITIONAL  for the reason xtime gives: the top bit is
; taken as a VALUE  0x87 is multiplied by it  and the exclusive or runs
; whatever that came to; Exclusive or with nought is the identity  so the
; branch SP 800_38B writes in prose costs nothing beyond the multiply  and
; the work does not depend on the value of the bit;
;
; IN PLACE; the value goes in at cell nought through cell fifteen and the
; answer comes back there; Everything above is scratch and is left clear
; which the exit contract states;
;
; THE DOUBLING NEEDS NO MASK  again for xtime's reason: a cell wraps at 256
; and the wrap IS the shift; What a byte needs from its neighbour is the
; neighbour's TOP BIT  which is why block/topbit is included sixteen times;
;
; TAPE MAP  (relative to the block's own zero)
;   @0x00:0x0f  v  the value  big endian  v at nought most significant
;   @0x10:0x1f  d  the doubling temps  spent back into v
;   @0x20:0x2f  h  the top bits; the one at nought triggers the reduction
;   @0x30:0x33  the block/topbit frame  byte q t f
;   @0x34:0x44  idiom/xor8 pasted at 0x34; result 0x34  operands 0x35 0x36
;
; ASSERT ptr=+0
; ASSERT zero +16:+68

; ==== every byte goes out twice: once to be doubled  once for its top bit ====
; byte 0 of sixteen
  [-R16+R32+L48]
; to the topbit frame
R48
; ASSERT ptr=+48
%%block/topbit%% 48
; and the bit goes to its place in h
  [-L16+R16]
L47
